================================================================================
KEY CONCEPTS EXPLANATION (VIVA REFERENCE):
================================================================================
1. Service Worker        : A client-side script running in the background separate from the web page, enabling resource caching, offline functionality, and background sync.
2. 'install' Event       : Fires once when the service worker is registered; uses caches.open() and cache.addAll() to cache key assets for offline use.
3. 'fetch' Event         : Intercepts network HTTP requests; checks the cache first with caches.match() and falls back to network fetch() if the resource is not cached.
4. manifest.json         : JSON configuration file providing app metadata (icons, display mode, theme colors) so the app can be installed on home screens.
5. localStorage          : Synchronous key-value client-side browser storage used here to persist the cart items locally even when the device is completely offline.
